        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-25 22:32:54.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20377 mgs: fix llog_catlist paging leak and duplicates",
        "message": "LU-20377 mgs: fix llog_catlist paging leak and duplicates\n\nWhen the ioctl buffer for \"lctl --device MGS llog_catlist\" filled\nup, mgs_list_logs() jumped to \"out\" with the rest of log_list still\nlinked, so those mgs_direntry entries were never freed.  An MGS with\nmany config logs would leak memory on every llog_catlist call.  The\nreturned ioc_count also pointed at the last listed log rather than\nthe next one, so that log was listed again at the start of the next\npage, and del_ost would process it twice.\n\nFree the remaining entries at \"out\", and return the index of the\nfirst log not yet listed.\n\nAlso free dentry_list in mgs_clear_configs() if allocating namedash\nfails.\n\nAdd conf-sanity test_123al to list enough logs for several pages.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=\"123af 123al\",ONLY_MINUTES=30\nFixes: 1d97a8b4cd3d (\"LU-13609 llog: list all the log files correctly on MGS/MDT\")\nFixes: 2a9518b1f820 (\"LU-8727 mgs: remove skip records from config file\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I04b43d2494ee2e360ed0f26ab4d382b5cf3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
